    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0658" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/5–1747: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Political Adviser in Korea</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Langdon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-17">May 17, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. Cite Zgbi 658. This headquarters yesterday, 15 May, released long message
                    from Representative Democratic Council to Secretary closing with a demand for
                    immediate withdrawal of occupation forces to make way for interim government in
                    process of being created by Koreans themselves.</p>
                <p>Department will recall RDC has lost its former quasi-official character and
                    become the tool of the most extreme and intransigent rightist element whose fate
                    is bound up in the <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi>. As for the message
                    it is understood that Dr. Rhee is aware of it and may have had a hand in
                    drafting it. To us this is an indication that the Rhee–Kim Koo “diehards” are
                    preparing a last desperate effort to embarrass, if not sabotage, the work of the
                    Joint Commission by resurrecting the trusteeship issue and exciting the
                    people.</p>
                <p>Recommend that the message be ignored. Our impression is that the vast majority
                    of Korean people and most newspapers are jubilant over the news of the
                    reconvening of the Joint Commission and prospect of national provisional
                    government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Langdon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
